WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.500
- I'm here with Cheryl Hines,

00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:03.700
and with us on Skype is Michelle Buteau.

00:00:03.700 --> 00:00:05.667
Give it up for them.

00:00:05.667 --> 00:00:07.470
I'm on with Cheryl and Michelle,

00:00:07.470 --> 00:00:11.040
both embrace the awkward
situations of life, as do I.

00:00:11.040 --> 00:00:13.860
We've all kind of made
careers out of it, in a way.

00:00:13.860 --> 00:00:15.640
So it's time to test what we'd do

00:00:15.640 --> 00:00:18.290
in a few awkward situations,
with a game called

00:00:18.290 --> 00:00:20.440
I'm Awesome At Being Awkward.

00:00:20.440 --> 00:00:25.270
- ♪ I'm awesome at being awkward. ♪

00:00:25.270 --> 00:00:26.438
(Kelly and Cheryl laughs)

00:00:26.438 --> 00:00:28.330
- Oh my god, I love my band.

00:00:28.330 --> 00:00:29.870
Here's what we do.

00:00:29.870 --> 00:00:33.330
When I say, "Go", our
super-random super-computer

00:00:33.330 --> 00:00:35.530
will flip through millions
of awkward situations

00:00:35.530 --> 00:00:38.360
and potential solutions
to those situations.

00:00:38.360 --> 00:00:42.110
We each have to say which
solution we would choose.

00:00:42.110 --> 00:00:43.450
Let's see what we've got.

00:00:43.450 --> 00:00:44.630
Go computer, go.

00:00:44.630 --> 00:00:47.313
(Computer makes noise
indicating it's working)

00:00:47.313 --> 00:00:48.146
(Computer dings)

00:00:48.146 --> 00:00:50.350
- Okay, so the person in the
dressing room next to you

00:00:50.350 --> 00:00:51.600
comes into your space.

00:00:51.600 --> 00:00:52.640
This has happened to me.

00:00:52.640 --> 00:00:55.510
Do you A: compliment her pants,

00:00:55.510 --> 00:00:58.210
B: cough loudly until she goes away.

00:00:58.210 --> 00:00:59.720
B all day.

00:00:59.720 --> 00:01:04.720
- Oh, I think I would do A,
sort of passive aggressive.

00:01:04.730 --> 00:01:06.230
- Passive aggressively.

00:01:06.230 --> 00:01:08.930
- Just like, "I like your pants...

00:01:10.230 --> 00:01:11.240
Yeah, but get."

00:01:13.890 --> 00:01:15.100
You'd be nice about it.

00:01:15.100 --> 00:01:17.200
- Yeah. What would you do, Michelle?

00:01:17.200 --> 00:01:18.932
- Be nice? Who has time to be nice?

00:01:18.932 --> 00:01:21.310
Get out of here. I need my space.

00:01:21.310 --> 00:01:22.143
You're making me feel

00:01:22.143 --> 00:01:25.000
that I'm in the middle
seat of an airplane. Go.

00:01:25.000 --> 00:01:26.350
- I hate that seat.

00:01:26.350 --> 00:01:29.087
No, I would cough loudly
until they go away.

00:01:29.087 --> 00:01:29.920
It's weird, too.

00:01:29.920 --> 00:01:30.753
- [Cheryl] It is weird.

00:01:30.753 --> 00:01:31.586
- It's just a weird thing to do.

00:01:31.586 --> 00:01:33.070
Like space, give space.

00:01:33.070 --> 00:01:34.696
Okay. Let's see the next one.

00:01:34.696 --> 00:01:37.369
(Computer makes noise
indicating it's working)

00:01:37.369 --> 00:01:38.202
(Computer dings)

00:01:38.202 --> 00:01:42.060
Okay, so you clog the toilet
at a house you're touring.

00:01:42.060 --> 00:01:46.430
Do you A: ask if the place
comes with a plunger,

00:01:46.430 --> 00:01:47.480
so you're owning it.

00:01:47.480 --> 00:01:50.383
B: blame it on someone else.

00:01:51.320 --> 00:01:53.020
What would you do, Michelle?

00:01:53.020 --> 00:01:57.252
- I'd have to blame it on
somebody else. (indistinct)

00:01:57.252 --> 00:02:00.763
I don't know what kind of
day they had. No, I can't.

00:02:00.763 --> 00:02:02.440
- That would be tough.

00:02:02.440 --> 00:02:04.930
I think you would have to
blame it on somebody else.

00:02:04.930 --> 00:02:07.820
- Oh my god, I'm the only
classless individual.

00:02:07.820 --> 00:02:09.040
I would just be like, "Dude.

00:02:09.040 --> 00:02:11.450
Okay, I just did
something, and it's there,

00:02:11.450 --> 00:02:13.500
and we're going to have to figure it out.

00:02:14.370 --> 00:02:15.640
You got a plunger?"

00:02:15.640 --> 00:02:18.056
- That's classy in its own way.

00:02:18.056 --> 00:02:20.950
- It's not. I should just leave.

00:02:20.950 --> 00:02:23.480
I should do B, but I totally would do A.

00:02:23.480 --> 00:02:25.293
Okay, next one. Let's see it.

00:02:25.293 --> 00:02:28.055
(Computer makes noise
indicating it's working)

00:02:28.055 --> 00:02:29.196
(Computer dings)

00:02:29.196 --> 00:02:30.080
- Okay. A stranger mistakes...

00:02:30.080 --> 00:02:30.913
Oh, this has happened.

00:02:30.913 --> 00:02:33.210
A stranger mistakes
you for another person.

00:02:33.210 --> 00:02:38.030
Do you A: roll with it, pretending
you are the other person,

00:02:38.030 --> 00:02:41.640
or B: embarrass the
stranger by correcting them.

00:02:41.640 --> 00:02:43.602
What would you do, Cheryl?

00:02:43.602 --> 00:02:45.250
- I have rolled with it.

00:02:45.250 --> 00:02:46.140
- [Kelly] I have as well.

00:02:46.140 --> 00:02:51.140
- Yeah. I was on a plane, and
this person came up and said,

00:02:51.207 --> 00:02:54.030
"Oh my gosh, I love you."

00:02:54.030 --> 00:02:55.950
And I said, "That's so nice. Thank you."

00:02:55.950 --> 00:02:57.770
They said, "I love Modern Family."

00:02:57.770 --> 00:03:01.030
And I said, "I do too."

00:03:01.030 --> 00:03:05.230
And they said, "Can I get my
picture with you, Julie Bowen?

00:03:05.230 --> 00:03:07.887
And I was like, "Yes."

00:03:09.363 --> 00:03:10.321
- I did the same.

00:03:10.321 --> 00:03:12.130
- [Cheryl] Did you?

00:03:12.130 --> 00:03:13.400
- Y'all look similar.

00:03:13.400 --> 00:03:15.190
I do not look like this person.

00:03:15.190 --> 00:03:16.617
This girl came up to me and was like,

00:03:16.617 --> 00:03:21.220
"Oh my god, your song 'So
Small' is one of my favorites."

00:03:21.220 --> 00:03:23.850
And I kept thinking, "I
don't have a song 'So Small.'

00:03:23.850 --> 00:03:25.690
And then she said another song.

00:03:25.690 --> 00:03:29.149
And I was like, "Oh, you
think I'm Carrie Underwood."

00:03:29.149 --> 00:03:33.123
And I literally look nothing
like Carrie Underwood.

00:03:34.850 --> 00:03:36.530
I was so embarrassed
for her that I just...

00:03:36.530 --> 00:03:37.990
She was like, "Can you sign this?"

00:03:37.990 --> 00:03:40.990
And I totally signed "Carrie Underwood."

00:03:42.687 --> 00:03:44.720
I think that might be illegal.

00:03:44.720 --> 00:03:46.880
- Just so you can get out of it.

00:03:46.880 --> 00:03:49.220
This one lady on the airplane one time

00:03:49.220 --> 00:03:51.340
thought I was Kim Cole.

00:03:51.340 --> 00:03:53.420
And I didn't know how
to tell her otherwise

00:03:53.420 --> 00:03:54.300
because she was kind of old.

00:03:54.300 --> 00:03:56.300
So I'm like, "Maybe
this is her dying wish."

00:03:56.300 --> 00:03:59.280
And so she just kept
asking me about TV stuff.

00:03:59.280 --> 00:04:00.190
I was like, "Yep."

00:04:00.190 --> 00:04:02.700
And at the end of the flight,
I just gave her an autograph.

00:04:02.700 --> 00:04:05.270
And I was like, "Have
fun, Esther, or Ethel,"

00:04:05.270 --> 00:04:06.520
whatever her name was.

00:04:06.520 --> 00:04:08.590
But sometimes you got to go with it.

00:04:08.590 --> 00:04:10.290
But I like putting people in their place,

00:04:10.290 --> 00:04:11.927
because I am not Raven-Symoné.

00:04:13.294 --> 00:04:14.767
- What? Do people say that?

00:04:14.767 --> 00:04:16.821
- That's not so Raven.

00:04:16.821 --> 00:04:18.957
(Kelly and Cheryl laugh)

00:04:18.957 --> 00:04:21.960
- That's awesome. I love you guys so much.

00:04:21.960 --> 00:04:23.060
That was awesome. I love the game.

00:04:23.060 --> 00:04:24.463
Thank you for playing.

